# Wesnoth Access end-to-end test: real game actions through the native code
# paths: select, move and attack (native attack dialog), recruit (native
# recruit dialog), end turn, enemy turn announcements.
#ARGS: -t access_test

never enemy Orcish Warrior
# (The hidden Elvish Ranger may legitimately reveal itself by attacking during
# the enemy turn, so it is only checked in map_basics.)

wait-for 180000 Your turn
wait-dialog 20000 transient_message
key Enter
wait 800

# Select the Spearman.
key F3
key F3
mark
key Enter
expect Selected your Spearman

# Choose the attack option from 6,3 and open the native attack dialog.
mark
key F7
expect from 6, 3
key Enter
wait-dialog 15000 unit_attack
expect Attack
mark
key F4
expect spear
# Confirm: the unit moves next to the Grunt and attacks.
mark
key Enter
wait-for 60000 attacks enemy Orcish Grunt
expect moved to 6, 3
expect to hit

# The fight gives the last experience point: the native advancement dialog
# lists the choices.
wait-dialog 60000 unit_advance
mark
key F4
expect Pikeman
expect Javelineer
expect Swordsman
mark
key Down
expect of 3
mark
key Enter
wait-for 20000 advanced to

# Recruit with the native dialog (Ctrl+R).
mark
key Shift+Home
expect Lieutenant
mark
key Ctrl+R
wait-dialog 15000 unit_recruit
expect Recruit
# The focus starts in the list of recruitable units.
expect list
mark
key Down
expect Spearman
mark
key Enter
wait-for 20000 recruited at
expect Spearman
expect gold 86

# Undo with the native key U is confirmed (or refused) by speech.
mark
key U
wait 1500
expect Undo

# End the turn (native Ctrl+Space); the enemy turn and the new turn are announced.
mark
key Ctrl+Space
wait-for 120000 Enemy turn
wait-for 180000 Your turn
expect Turn 2 of 10

quit
